son_slug":"penny-wright","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions — Forestry","noes":35,"question":"Christine Milne I, and also on behalf of Senator Bob Brown, move: That the Senate— (a) notes: (i) clauses 25 and 27 of the Tasmanian Forests Intergovernmental Agreement between the Commonwealth of Australia and the State of Tasmania (IGA), signed by Prime Minister Gillard, and (ii) that current logging and proposed logging in the 430 000 hectares of high conservation forests proposed for protection breaches these clauses of the IGA; and (b) calls on the Government to immediately honour the IGA. Richard Colbeck by leave—I move: Paragraph (b), omit “honour”, substitute “abandon”. Stephen Parry The question is that the amendment moved by Senator Colbeck be agreed to. Joe Ludwig I seek leave to make a short statement. Stephen Parry Leave is granted for two minutes. Joe Ludwig We object to the amendment. Clearly the opposition want to abandon the agreement. This would be a complete disaster for jobs in Tasmania and a disaster for a strong regional future in Australia. The opposition stand not to support the intergovernmental agreement. They move away from forestry in Tasmania. It has been a decision by individual businesses, not a decision by government. It has happened regardless of government. The opposition seek to abandon the agreement. That would take away a significant amount of support that Tasmania deserves. It would take away $40 million in assistance to workers and timber communities, $45 million in support for contractors and $120 million for regional areas in Tasmania and transition to a long-term sustainable future. I will just make a brief comment in respect of Senator Milne's substantive motion. The intergovernmental agreement on Tasmanian forestry is well underway. Governments are working with industry, environmental groups and the CFMEU in Tasmania to progress the agreement. It has been a community led agreement from the start, and we commend those parties for coming to the table to end the decades of conflict. The government cannot support the motion. I","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-2137","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2011-11-02/6"}
